{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLHcmoWWemF2brjPKcn4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`trigsimp` now turns the first example into `sin(k)`. It also turns the second into `sin(k)/k`, but I haven't made it return `sinc(k)`.\n\nThe change is in `futrig` in `sympy/simplify/trigsimp.py`. After the usual simplification, if the result still contains `exp`, it rewrites the expression into trig form and simplifies that. It keeps the trig version only if it has fewer operations. This leaves cases that don't improve alone: `trigsimp(exp(I*k))` still gives `exp(I*k)`, and `exp(k)+exp(-k)` still gives `2*cosh(k)`.\n\nI ran `test_trigsimp.py` and `test_simplify.py`. Three tests fail: `test_issue_6811_fail`, `test_factorial_simplify` and `test_simplify_float_vs_integer`. The same three fail on a clean checkout without my change, so they aren't caused by it. I didn't add tests for the new behaviour, since I wasn't to touch test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":562,"cache_read_input_tokens":25671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":562},"output_tokens":341,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b0a7a3-3156-4031-83d2-ea5b3f5638fb","uuid":"a5b16fa2-d8ee-4165-9749-345c6d5e5b5d","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:53:35.028Z","request_id":"req_011ChLHcmfKMtJaPhVJYrtzi"}
